WEBVTT

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:05.430
Are we sure he is well?

00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:08.380
I tried to talk to him, but he doesn't respond at all.

00:00:09.490 --> 00:00:12.500
Can this truly happen to a person,

00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:15.500
merely for going a week without any punishment?

00:00:15.830 --> 00:00:23.880
Punishment...

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:27.360
Be back by suppertime at 6:30.

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:30.260
If you don't come back, your tardiness will be considered a breakout.

00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:31.140
Are you sure?

00:00:31.790 --> 00:00:34.270
I haven't really done that much lately.

00:00:34.270 --> 00:00:35.470
What's wrong with you?

00:00:35.470 --> 00:00:36.820
Don't you want to go out?

00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:37.350
No!

00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:39.920
I will accept your kindness with pleasure!

00:00:42.440 --> 00:00:44.170
Punishment...

00:00:44.170 --> 00:00:46.130
Poor Andre.

00:00:46.130 --> 00:00:49.560
Why is Andre the only one the
vice president isn't punishing?

00:00:49.560 --> 00:00:52.450
I have to say, lots of strange things have been happening lately.

00:00:53.790 --> 00:00:55.110
Shingo.

00:00:55.110 --> 00:00:57.580
What?! Don't shout at me out of nowhere like that!

00:00:57.580 --> 00:00:59.420
Oh... Sorry.

00:00:59.420 --> 00:01:03.530
Listen, the vice president's
been fetching you a lot lately.

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:04.330
Is everything okay?

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:06.560
Huh? What are you talking about?

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:08.970
I mean, as long as she's not
doing anything to you, but...

00:01:09.510 --> 00:01:13.060
Lately, the Underground Student
Council has been acting strangely.

00:01:13.390 --> 00:01:17.430
So I thought to ask you to let me know if they're doing anything to you.

00:01:17.430 --> 00:01:19.480
If so, I'd like to help.

00:01:19.480 --> 00:01:21.920
Shingo! Come with me to the Corrections Office!

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:22.440
Yes.

00:01:25.940 --> 00:01:28.640
I can be back by 6:30 with time to spare.

00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:29.740
Here.

00:01:29.740 --> 00:01:31.240
What are you spacing out for?

00:01:31.470 --> 00:01:33.090
Oh, no reason.

00:01:33.090 --> 00:01:34.570
Hold mine, too.

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:37.210
Excuse me, coming through.

00:01:39.210 --> 00:01:40.290
Holy crap!

00:01:40.650 --> 00:01:42.750
I can't wait to see these "grapes of wrath."

00:01:42.750 --> 00:01:44.320
Yeah, me, too.

00:01:44.320 --> 00:01:47.100
I wonder how the grapes are gonna attack people.

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:47.630
What?

00:01:47.630 --> 00:01:49.590
Don't tell me you're freaking out.

00:01:49.590 --> 00:01:51.080
I'm not freaking out!

00:01:51.080 --> 00:01:51.730
If anyone, <i>you're</i>—

00:01:51.730 --> 00:01:53.100
Shh! It's starting.

00:01:53.360 --> 00:01:54.350
From now on,

00:01:54.720 --> 00:01:57.200
I want you to service
the barricade's entrance!

00:01:57.900 --> 00:02:00.600
Oh, carrying out your club's activities here, are you?

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:01.990
Ah, mm-hmm.

00:02:01.990 --> 00:02:04.440
The weather's nice today, so we're playing outside.

00:02:04.810 --> 00:02:06.760
Nice and refined, isn't it?

00:02:06.760 --> 00:02:07.440
Well then...

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:08.030
Right!

00:02:16.490 --> 00:02:18.370
Is this really that badly put together?

00:02:20.080 --> 00:02:23.610
Is Andre-dono not going to shower again today?

00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:24.440
Nope.

00:02:24.440 --> 00:02:25.670
I tried talking to him,

00:02:25.940 --> 00:02:28.090
but he's sitting unresponsive in the corner of his room again.

00:02:28.730 --> 00:02:31.670
I was so nervous the vice president would notice.

00:02:31.670 --> 00:02:34.660
Thanks for your help, Mayumi.

00:02:34.660 --> 00:02:36.940
Do you think your message got through to him?

00:02:36.940 --> 00:02:37.680
It's all right.

00:02:38.060 --> 00:02:40.580
Just for a second, when
we made eye contact,

00:02:40.580 --> 00:02:42.560
I could tell I got through to him.

00:02:42.940 --> 00:02:45.820
"Kick plan they to you out..."

00:02:46.070 --> 00:02:47.900
What on earth does that mean?

00:02:48.180 --> 00:02:49.560
Punishment...

00:02:49.560 --> 00:02:50.540
Whipping...

00:02:50.540 --> 00:02:51.150
Spitting...

00:02:51.690 --> 00:02:52.690
Punishment...

00:02:52.690 --> 00:02:55.370
Andre...

00:02:55.670 --> 00:02:57.790
Punishment time...

00:02:58.390 --> 00:03:00.120
Andre...

00:03:00.930 --> 00:03:03.090
Punishment time...

00:03:03.860 --> 00:03:06.260
Andre...

00:04:40.660 --> 00:04:42.890
Hey, isn't this movie really boring?

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:45.890
Uh, well, yeah, it is.

00:04:45.890 --> 00:04:47.770
Let's get out of here, already.

00:04:49.130 --> 00:04:49.520
Hey,

00:04:50.010 --> 00:04:52.270
you've still got time, right?

00:04:52.270 --> 00:04:53.480
Yeah.

00:04:53.710 --> 00:04:54.990
A little more than an hour.

00:04:55.280 --> 00:04:56.710
Where should we go?

00:04:56.710 --> 00:04:58.830
Let's find some food. My treat.

00:04:58.830 --> 00:05:01.320
Hey, that's okay. Don't overdo it.

00:05:01.320 --> 00:05:02.830
There's a park over there.

00:05:02.830 --> 00:05:04.160
Let's go.

00:05:04.160 --> 00:05:06.980
Andre...

00:05:06.980 --> 00:05:09.470
Punishment time...

00:05:09.470 --> 00:05:11.500
Andre...

00:05:11.500 --> 00:05:14.170
Punishment time...

00:05:14.420 --> 00:05:15.970
Vice President...!

00:05:16.400 --> 00:05:18.840
Please punish me, Vice President!

00:05:21.720 --> 00:05:23.230
No...

00:05:33.990 --> 00:05:36.260
What is my diary doing here?

00:05:37.700 --> 00:05:41.050
"I was in the corner of the room, feeling sorry for myself as usual,

00:05:41.050 --> 00:05:44.370
when I heard a voice come out of nowhere, saying "Punishment time."

00:05:44.870 --> 00:05:46.660
I followed the voice but,

00:05:46.660 --> 00:05:49.210
all I found was a cardboard cutout of the vice president, and I was disappointed."

00:05:49.610 --> 00:05:52.210
This is what just happened...!

00:05:52.640 --> 00:05:56.340
"The door inside the Corrections Office was open, and past the door

00:05:56.340 --> 00:05:58.540
was the vice president!

00:05:58.540 --> 00:06:01.550
I was finally able to
get plenty of punishment."

00:06:04.520 --> 00:06:05.470
If I go...

00:06:06.080 --> 00:06:07.520
through that door...

00:06:08.170 --> 00:06:09.380
Kiyoshi-dono...

00:06:10.180 --> 00:06:12.320
Is something troubling you?

00:06:12.320 --> 00:06:16.070
Listen, does "Kick plan they to you out..." mean anything?

00:06:16.070 --> 00:06:18.840
Huh? What is that?

00:06:18.840 --> 00:06:20.890
A spell cast with a sentence backwards?

00:06:20.890 --> 00:06:21.990
No...

00:06:21.990 --> 00:06:23.490
It was written like this.

00:06:25.450 --> 00:06:27.570
What an ominous missive!

00:06:27.570 --> 00:06:27.910
Huh?

00:06:28.510 --> 00:06:30.650
Read it from top-to-bottom!

00:06:30.650 --> 00:06:32.170
"They plan to...

00:06:32.750 --> 00:06:33.880
kick you out!"

00:06:34.230 --> 00:06:36.290
What does that mean, kick us out?

00:06:36.290 --> 00:06:39.230
Why would that sprout up all of a sudden?!

00:06:39.230 --> 00:06:42.810
It may have to do with all the strange
things that have been happening lately.

00:06:42.810 --> 00:06:46.850
If those things have been set up all along to drive us out of school...

00:06:47.210 --> 00:06:48.450
Set up by who?

00:06:48.450 --> 00:06:50.700
It could only be by the
Underground Student Council!

00:06:51.750 --> 00:06:52.560
Andre!

00:06:54.930 --> 00:06:57.480
It's the real vice president!

00:06:58.190 --> 00:06:59.070
Andre!

00:06:59.380 --> 00:07:00.450
Kiyoshi-dono!

00:07:01.300 --> 00:07:02.490
Come hither!

00:07:07.010 --> 00:07:11.000
Who are you calling your mom?!

00:07:11.000 --> 00:07:12.360
Huh?!

00:07:14.350 --> 00:07:15.440
Andre...

00:07:16.100 --> 00:07:17.130
you're going to need...

00:07:18.060 --> 00:07:20.720
some severe punishment.

00:07:21.540 --> 00:07:22.520
Mom—!

00:07:22.520 --> 00:07:24.680
I mean, Vice President!

00:07:24.680 --> 00:07:27.680
You "accidentally" called
me "Mom" again?!

00:07:28.310 --> 00:07:31.680
Please! Punish me!

00:07:32.230 --> 00:07:33.300
What's the matter?

00:07:33.300 --> 00:07:34.270
I can't reach you.

00:07:34.590 --> 00:07:36.650
I can't punish you like this, can I?

00:07:36.880 --> 00:07:37.940
Well, what's the matter?

00:07:39.870 --> 00:07:40.460
Andre!

00:07:40.460 --> 00:07:40.820
Stop!

00:07:41.130 --> 00:07:42.490
Don't do it!

00:07:49.350 --> 00:07:50.240
Why you...

00:07:50.240 --> 00:07:51.000
fat pig!

00:07:51.330 --> 00:07:54.430
Thank you very much!

00:07:54.430 --> 00:07:55.460
Prison break!

00:07:55.460 --> 00:07:57.790
No way! I didn't break out!

00:07:58.220 --> 00:07:59.380
Hold still!

00:07:59.760 --> 00:08:00.650
Andre...

00:08:00.650 --> 00:08:02.760
Kiyoshi-dono, look at this.

00:08:02.760 --> 00:08:05.950
These look as if they were cut
partway through with wire cutters.

00:08:05.950 --> 00:08:06.760
We've been had!

00:08:07.530 --> 00:08:09.140
The Underground Student Council set us up!

00:08:09.660 --> 00:08:11.400
That went well, didn't it?

00:08:11.400 --> 00:08:12.140
Yes.

00:08:12.140 --> 00:08:16.150
Imagine, a use such as this
for an overstuffed uniform!

00:08:16.530 --> 00:08:19.940
Wind up Andre, already at the brink, to a fever pitch,

00:08:19.940 --> 00:08:22.450
and then have him break through the barricade.

00:08:22.450 --> 00:08:24.110
It went just as you planned.

00:08:24.570 --> 00:08:27.610
You did well to handle squeezing into that tight uniform.

00:08:27.610 --> 00:08:29.310
No, not at all.

00:08:29.310 --> 00:08:30.030
Now...

00:08:30.360 --> 00:08:33.000
...we simply wait for the snitch to return.

00:08:33.240 --> 00:08:35.840
So "The Grapes of Wrath"
wasn't a horror movie, huh?

00:08:35.840 --> 00:08:39.220
To be honest, I fell asleep less than 30 minutes into it.

00:08:39.220 --> 00:08:40.750
You gave up too fast!

00:08:40.750 --> 00:08:43.090
And to think I was trying to stay awake!

00:08:43.090 --> 00:08:44.210
I'm really sorry.

00:08:44.210 --> 00:08:44.920
Man...

00:08:46.050 --> 00:08:47.460
Pinchy-pinchy!

00:08:47.460 --> 00:08:48.810
I'm so happy!

00:08:48.810 --> 00:08:50.430
I'm beyond happy!

00:08:50.860 --> 00:08:54.430
And, the way things are headed,
I might score even more happiness...

00:08:54.950 --> 00:08:55.860
meaning...

00:08:56.660 --> 00:08:58.810
I might land a kiss...

00:08:58.810 --> 00:08:59.650
Yikes!

00:08:59.650 --> 00:09:00.280
Huh?

00:09:00.280 --> 00:09:02.320
What, are you angry?

00:09:02.320 --> 00:09:04.430
You just made a really creepy face.

00:09:04.430 --> 00:09:06.020
I ain't angry!

00:09:06.020 --> 00:09:07.910
In fact, I'm really happy.

00:09:07.910 --> 00:09:09.560
Huh? You're happy?

00:09:09.560 --> 00:09:10.910
Er, no...

00:09:10.910 --> 00:09:13.160
Why would you make a face like that if you're feeling happy?

00:09:13.160 --> 00:09:16.230
That's the face you make when you get your cheeks pinched.

00:09:16.230 --> 00:09:17.370
Really?

00:09:18.080 --> 00:09:20.080
Let's see then, you pinch my cheeks.

00:09:20.080 --> 00:09:20.880
Huh?

00:09:22.880 --> 00:09:25.170
Well? Does my face look creepy?

00:09:27.300 --> 00:09:29.500
What? Say something!

00:09:41.560 --> 00:09:43.570
Ah, I can't watch anymore!

00:09:44.180 --> 00:09:46.440
What are you throwing sand at him for?!

00:09:46.440 --> 00:09:48.250
It could get in his eyes, you know!

00:09:48.250 --> 00:09:49.190
That's okay!

00:09:49.190 --> 00:09:50.710
I mean, it's his own fault!

00:09:50.710 --> 00:09:53.240
He ditched us and went
off to play with a girl!

00:09:53.240 --> 00:09:55.550
He can do that if he wants, can't he?

00:09:55.550 --> 00:09:56.470
No he can't!

00:09:56.470 --> 00:09:58.750
We made a rule that says "no playing with girls"!

00:09:58.750 --> 00:09:59.950
You traitor!

00:09:59.950 --> 00:10:01.500
I said stop that!

00:10:05.120 --> 00:10:07.460
Ah... I'm sorry I yelled at you.

00:10:08.630 --> 00:10:12.400
But it's not very manly to pick on someone like that.

00:10:12.400 --> 00:10:14.660
If he's your friend, then forgive him.

00:10:15.860 --> 00:10:16.810
What was that for?!

00:10:16.810 --> 00:10:17.930
Don't bully them!

00:10:18.730 --> 00:10:19.840
Let's go, guys!

00:10:19.840 --> 00:10:21.020
Yeah!

00:10:22.850 --> 00:10:24.950
Kids, right?

00:10:24.950 --> 00:10:27.430
Still, it all worked
out in the end, didn't it?

00:10:27.430 --> 00:10:29.070
It looks like they
made up and everything.

00:10:29.420 --> 00:10:32.540
Way to go, Shingo.

00:10:32.540 --> 00:10:34.280
That was pretty cool.

00:10:35.990 --> 00:10:37.040
"If he's your friend...

00:10:39.150 --> 00:10:41.400
then forgive him," huh?

00:10:43.260 --> 00:10:45.960
Saying that after not
forgiving him one bit...

00:10:45.960 --> 00:10:47.020
Huh?

00:10:47.020 --> 00:10:48.550
What is it? What's wrong?

00:10:49.200 --> 00:10:50.760
The truth is,

00:10:51.190 --> 00:10:53.890
I've been let out lately in return

00:10:53.890 --> 00:10:55.680
for spilling information on the others to the vice president!

00:10:56.890 --> 00:10:59.390
They've been doing prison labor,

00:10:59.390 --> 00:11:01.380
while I've been going to the arcade,

00:11:01.380 --> 00:11:03.190
and fooling around with you, Anzu.

00:11:03.190 --> 00:11:04.610
I'm the worst.

00:11:05.290 --> 00:11:07.450
This is a full-blown breakout.

00:11:07.450 --> 00:11:09.280
It was you guys that
lured him out, wasn't it?!

00:11:09.650 --> 00:11:11.280
You all saw him, didn't you?

00:11:11.660 --> 00:11:14.400
Andre broke out all on his own.

00:11:14.400 --> 00:11:16.160
Guys, I'm sorry...

00:11:16.490 --> 00:11:19.870
This is the second breakout, following Kiyoshi's.

00:11:19.870 --> 00:11:21.760
According to the Underground Student Council regulations,

00:11:21.760 --> 00:11:24.920
your sentences are to be extended by three more months.

00:11:25.590 --> 00:11:28.060
Sorry to bore you with all of this.

00:11:28.060 --> 00:11:30.010
It's still early, but I'm heading back to the school.

00:11:30.010 --> 00:11:31.880
I want to apologize to everyone.

00:11:32.310 --> 00:11:34.820
And I don't want to embarrass myself any more than this.

00:11:36.010 --> 00:11:38.450
I'm so sorry... Shingo...

00:11:42.440 --> 00:11:46.540
I've... done something I have to apologize to you for, Shingo.

00:11:46.540 --> 00:11:47.270
Huh?

00:11:47.810 --> 00:11:49.640
Come to think of it, where's Shingo?

00:11:49.640 --> 00:11:53.450
I told him to be back by 6:30, but he sure is taking his time.

00:11:53.950 --> 00:11:57.030
I told him that if he's one
minute and one second late,

00:11:57.030 --> 00:11:58.650
his tardiness will be
counted as a breakout.

00:11:58.650 --> 00:12:00.370
You mean you set a
trap for Shingo, too?!

00:12:01.460 --> 00:12:04.440
Where on <i>earth</i> could
he be traipsing around?

00:12:06.260 --> 00:12:09.030
Are you content with
your current position?

00:12:09.030 --> 00:12:10.270
Y-Yes.

00:12:10.270 --> 00:12:14.080
I am greatly honored to be able to support the Underground Student Council

00:12:14.080 --> 00:12:15.470
as Captain of the Guard.

00:12:16.240 --> 00:12:17.050
Anzu-san,

00:12:18.010 --> 00:12:20.510
would you be interested in an executive post next term?

00:12:20.510 --> 00:12:22.510
That, I couldn't...

00:12:23.410 --> 00:12:24.350
Anzu-san...

00:12:25.010 --> 00:12:27.230
There is a certain task I'd like you to do.

00:12:27.230 --> 00:12:29.230
If you are successful...

00:12:31.660 --> 00:12:33.860
I will recommend you.

00:12:33.860 --> 00:12:38.070
And so, I was told to get friendly with you outside of school.

00:12:38.850 --> 00:12:40.780
Are you... serious?

00:12:41.050 --> 00:12:43.000
It was all for today.

00:12:43.770 --> 00:12:46.010
If I kept you here, Shingo,

00:12:46.010 --> 00:12:49.130
and made sure you didn't get back to the school in time,

00:12:49.130 --> 00:12:51.730
the boys would have committed a third breakout,

00:12:51.730 --> 00:12:53.010
and you'd all be expelled!

00:12:53.010 --> 00:12:53.920
Expelled?!

00:12:53.920 --> 00:12:55.540
The Underground Student Council set you up.

00:12:55.540 --> 00:12:57.770
There's no time! Hurry back, now!

00:12:57.770 --> 00:12:59.850
I'm not sure I get it all, but all right!

00:13:00.840 --> 00:13:01.970
There's time if I run back—

00:13:01.970 --> 00:13:03.970
No! That watch is 30 minutes behind!

00:13:04.290 --> 00:13:06.390
I set it back at the movie theater!

00:13:06.390 --> 00:13:08.270
Huh...? Then, right now, it's...!

00:13:10.500 --> 00:13:12.110
6:25.

00:13:12.420 --> 00:13:13.900
Only five more minutes.

00:13:13.900 --> 00:13:15.610
There is not enough time!

00:13:15.610 --> 00:13:16.840
Oh, no!

00:13:16.840 --> 00:13:18.360
We're done for.

00:13:19.470 --> 00:13:20.620
I'm sure he'll get here.

00:13:21.220 --> 00:13:23.370
I'm sure Shingo will be back in time.

00:13:23.620 --> 00:13:24.580
Based on what?!

00:13:24.580 --> 00:13:25.830
All we can do is believe, right?!

00:13:26.220 --> 00:13:27.580
Believe in him...

00:13:27.850 --> 00:13:29.960
and wait here for Shingo!

00:13:31.040 --> 00:13:35.050
Only four more minutes until you're all expelled.

00:13:35.980 --> 00:13:37.670
What a shame, huh?

00:13:38.100 --> 00:13:40.410
We hold seaside school during the summer,

00:13:40.410 --> 00:13:43.030
where we have campfires and barbecue,

00:13:43.030 --> 00:13:44.970
hold a wet T-shirt contest,

00:13:44.970 --> 00:13:48.050
and a plethora of other fun events.

00:13:48.050 --> 00:13:49.400
...contest?!

00:13:50.430 --> 00:13:53.230
No, Shingo-kun will
make it back in time.

00:13:53.510 --> 00:13:55.010
All we can do is believe.

00:13:55.010 --> 00:13:55.730
I believe!

00:13:55.730 --> 00:13:58.860
Guys, let's reach out to him, with all our hearts!

00:13:59.420 --> 00:14:02.110
Shingo! Come back!

00:14:02.110 --> 00:14:03.910
Come back!

00:14:10.220 --> 00:14:12.210
Shingo!

00:14:13.160 --> 00:14:14.800
Stop shouting! Be quiet!

00:14:14.800 --> 00:14:16.290
Shingo-dono!

00:14:16.290 --> 00:14:18.340
Come back!

00:14:18.340 --> 00:14:20.030
Why, you...!

00:14:20.030 --> 00:14:22.430
Vice President, leave them be.

00:14:23.000 --> 00:14:24.600
As long as Anzu keeps him over there,

00:14:24.600 --> 00:14:27.300
the snitch will not be coming back.

00:14:27.300 --> 00:14:28.560
Hey, are you okay?!

00:14:28.970 --> 00:14:30.890
I-I'm all right.

00:14:30.890 --> 00:14:33.400
I just fell down... you didn't hit me.

00:14:33.400 --> 00:14:35.710
Never mind that, what time is it?!

00:14:38.630 --> 00:14:40.200
Scream! Scream!

00:14:40.200 --> 00:14:41.630
Scream away!

00:14:41.630 --> 00:14:46.740
One more minute, and we will get our peaceful school life back.

00:14:50.040 --> 00:14:51.000
Thanks, Pops!

00:14:51.000 --> 00:14:51.840
It's Shingo!

00:14:51.840 --> 00:14:52.580
Shingo-kun!

00:14:52.580 --> 00:14:54.040
He finally got here, huh?

00:14:54.040 --> 00:14:56.810
That's the old gent from the cleaners!

00:14:56.810 --> 00:14:57.340
How...?

00:14:57.340 --> 00:14:58.270
Shingo, hurry!

00:14:58.270 --> 00:14:58.960
Shingo-kun!

00:14:58.960 --> 00:15:00.210
There is no time!

00:15:00.210 --> 00:15:01.050
What's the time?!

00:15:01.050 --> 00:15:02.260
30 more seconds!

00:15:02.260 --> 00:15:03.390
It's okay! He's gonna make it!

00:15:04.290 --> 00:15:04.970
He did it!

00:15:05.760 --> 00:15:06.160
Guys!

00:15:06.160 --> 00:15:07.260
Ten seconds left.

00:15:08.520 --> 00:15:09.310
What are you waiting for?!

00:15:09.310 --> 00:15:10.190
Hurry and open it!

00:15:10.190 --> 00:15:11.140
I know! But something's—

00:15:11.140 --> 00:15:12.230
It won't open!

00:15:12.230 --> 00:15:13.420
Shingo, no!

00:15:13.420 --> 00:15:14.100
The door opens—

00:15:18.230 --> 00:15:19.030
Zero.

00:15:20.400 --> 00:15:21.570
Time over.

00:15:24.680 --> 00:15:27.330
Screw that! Locking the door isn't fair!

00:15:27.330 --> 00:15:28.610
What are you talking about?

00:15:28.610 --> 00:15:31.540
The door opens like this, right?

00:15:31.800 --> 00:15:33.390
No way...

00:15:33.390 --> 00:15:34.290
Since when...?

00:15:34.630 --> 00:15:36.500
It was badly put-together, you see.

00:15:36.500 --> 00:15:38.840
These boys fixed it for us.

00:15:38.840 --> 00:15:41.050
Damn it, so <i>that's</i> what that was about!

00:15:43.290 --> 00:15:45.470
This makes it your third breakout.

00:15:45.470 --> 00:15:49.060
As such, you will all be expelled.

00:15:49.060 --> 00:15:49.880
Did you hear?

00:15:49.880 --> 00:15:52.500
The boys broke out two
times yesterday alone.

00:15:52.500 --> 00:15:54.060
That means they're expelled, right?

00:15:54.440 --> 00:15:57.150
It'll be a relief to not have those nasty boys around anymore.

00:15:58.410 --> 00:15:59.860
Shingo...

00:15:59.860 --> 00:16:00.690
I'm sorry.

00:16:01.410 --> 00:16:04.460
You were seeing a girl outside?

00:16:04.460 --> 00:16:08.260
And after ragging on Kiyoshi over
doing the same thing, too, Shingo.

00:16:08.260 --> 00:16:13.020
Not to mention that the girl was a kunoichi of the Underground Student Council.

00:16:13.700 --> 00:16:15.120
I really am sorry.

00:16:15.120 --> 00:16:18.030
Guys, you can all beat me until you're satisfied.

00:16:18.030 --> 00:16:18.820
Please do so!

00:16:21.490 --> 00:16:22.420
Stand up, Shingo.

00:16:24.510 --> 00:16:26.510
When my breakout was discovered,

00:16:26.510 --> 00:16:29.400
you hit me, remember?

00:16:29.400 --> 00:16:30.180
Kiyoshi-dono!

00:16:30.180 --> 00:16:33.140
Yeah. So hit me as hard as you want.

00:16:33.140 --> 00:16:34.960
Okay, don't mind if I do.

00:16:40.280 --> 00:16:42.140
Now we're even.

00:16:42.140 --> 00:16:43.250
Kiyoshi...

00:16:44.870 --> 00:16:47.690
We're all equally guilty.

00:16:48.190 --> 00:16:51.490
No one here could hit you for real.

00:16:51.490 --> 00:16:53.120
Verily.

00:16:53.120 --> 00:16:55.810
Shingo-dono, you were set up by
the Underground Student Council,

00:16:55.810 --> 00:16:58.430
and had your manly
feelings toyed around with.

00:16:58.890 --> 00:17:00.590
If anything, we feel sorry for you.

00:17:00.590 --> 00:17:02.940
Shingo-kun, you apologized.

00:17:02.940 --> 00:17:04.460
That's good enough for me.

00:17:04.460 --> 00:17:06.930
Well, Kiyoshi does have a point.

00:17:07.980 --> 00:17:08.780
I...

00:17:10.980 --> 00:17:13.340
I did all those terrible things...

00:17:13.340 --> 00:17:14.890
I betrayed you all...

00:17:16.480 --> 00:17:18.350
Thank you, guys...

00:17:19.930 --> 00:17:23.240
You know, Shingo-dono, when you were rushing back full-tilt,

00:17:23.240 --> 00:17:24.740
yours truly was quite moved.

00:17:25.320 --> 00:17:29.650
It's because Anzu confessed her part in this that I got back at the time I did.

00:17:30.860 --> 00:17:31.580
Ho...

00:17:31.810 --> 00:17:33.280
"Anzu"?

00:17:33.280 --> 00:17:36.080
You are already on terms close
enough to not warrant suffixes?

00:17:36.370 --> 00:17:37.830
Yeah, well...

00:17:37.830 --> 00:17:41.040
We hold hands, and pinch each other's cheeks, and stuff.

00:17:43.380 --> 00:17:44.380
You did <i>that</i> much?

00:17:44.970 --> 00:17:48.340
But it was all part of her trap,
so you couldn't help it, right?

00:17:48.340 --> 00:17:50.130
Well, I guess so.

00:17:50.130 --> 00:17:54.060
The downblouse and nip-slip might
also have been part of the trap, too.

00:17:54.920 --> 00:17:58.190
But in the end, she confessed to me the truth about everything.

00:17:58.190 --> 00:18:01.490
So I feel like I really shared a connection with Anzu.

00:18:07.440 --> 00:18:10.030
You said you wouldn't hit me for real...

00:18:10.360 --> 00:18:13.240
Seeing nipples is too serious of a crime.

00:18:13.240 --> 00:18:14.330
Indeed it is.

00:18:14.330 --> 00:18:17.130
Though you did see those nipples as part of the Underground Student Council's setup,

00:18:17.130 --> 00:18:19.040
I am much too envious to not care.

00:18:19.040 --> 00:18:20.770
If you saw nipples,

00:18:20.770 --> 00:18:22.500
then just apologizing isn't good enough.

00:18:22.500 --> 00:18:24.250
You saw nipples, after all.

00:18:24.660 --> 00:18:26.800
Now we really are even.

00:18:29.340 --> 00:18:31.840
Gentlemen, I'm pleased to meet...

00:18:32.690 --> 00:18:33.390
you!

00:18:33.950 --> 00:18:35.530
Pleased to meet you.

00:18:35.530 --> 00:18:38.460
I did not expect that we would have to meet like this.

00:18:38.940 --> 00:18:41.690
You know the reason why you were called in here today...

00:18:41.690 --> 00:18:42.170
right?

00:18:42.170 --> 00:18:44.050
Onee-chan set them up!

00:18:44.050 --> 00:18:45.980
Chiyo, I will listen to what you have to say after—

00:18:45.980 --> 00:18:48.440
I saw it in the Underground Student Council room!

00:18:48.440 --> 00:18:52.430
A document with "DTO: Dog Transferal Operation" written on it!

00:18:52.430 --> 00:18:55.070
Mari, is what she's saying...

00:18:55.070 --> 00:18:55.410
true?!

00:18:55.410 --> 00:18:57.080
She must be mistaken.

00:18:57.080 --> 00:18:59.790
I have never seen
nor heard of such a thing.

00:19:00.210 --> 00:19:03.080
Without any proof, no explanation is warranted.

00:19:03.900 --> 00:19:07.090
If that's all you have to say, then run along, Chiyo.

00:19:08.460 --> 00:19:11.260
I'm sorry I couldn't be of any help, Kiyoshi-kun.

00:19:11.910 --> 00:19:12.760
Chiyo-chan...

00:19:13.660 --> 00:19:18.270
In accordance with the Underground Student
Council regulations, you are all to be expelled.

00:19:18.270 --> 00:19:19.060
Isn't that right, Chairman?

00:19:20.690 --> 00:19:22.310
According to the regulations...

00:19:22.940 --> 00:19:23.640
yes!

00:19:24.310 --> 00:19:27.490
This matter will be discussed at
next week's committee meeting,

00:19:27.490 --> 00:19:32.050
and will be finalized with the chairman
affixing his seal to the expulsion papers.

00:19:32.880 --> 00:19:35.170
When are you planning to affix your seal?

00:19:37.260 --> 00:19:39.500
Chairman! Rules are rules!

00:19:39.500 --> 00:19:40.750
When will you affix your seal?!

00:19:42.030 --> 00:19:45.960
The end of the week
after next, at the latest.

00:19:46.890 --> 00:19:49.880
Wow, the DTO really worked, huh?

00:19:49.880 --> 00:19:51.670
You masterfully carried it out.

00:19:52.650 --> 00:19:54.520
Now, a toast.

00:19:54.520 --> 00:19:56.260
To the boys being expelled.

00:19:56.260 --> 00:19:57.720
Cheers!

00:19:58.040 --> 00:20:01.760
All right, in celebration of the DTO's great success,

00:20:01.760 --> 00:20:03.770
if I may be so bold, a small performance.

00:20:04.940 --> 00:20:08.440
Watch as I do 50 pull-ups using only my fingers.

00:20:08.990 --> 00:20:09.980
One.

00:20:11.450 --> 00:20:12.440
Two.

00:20:14.700 --> 00:20:15.510
Three.

00:20:15.510 --> 00:20:17.880
Come to think of it, how did Shingo make it back by curfew, anyway?

00:20:17.880 --> 00:20:18.960
Four.

00:20:18.960 --> 00:20:21.080
I will call Anzu in and ask her about that matter.

00:20:22.070 --> 00:20:23.290
Forty-seven.

00:20:24.110 --> 00:20:25.430
Forty-eight.

00:20:25.430 --> 00:20:27.090
Only two more to go.

00:20:27.090 --> 00:20:28.730
Hang in there, Vice President!

00:20:28.730 --> 00:20:30.370
You're almost there!

00:20:30.370 --> 00:20:31.880
Forty-nine.

00:20:34.470 --> 00:20:36.380
Fifty—

00:20:36.380 --> 00:20:37.220
Please excuse me.

00:20:39.120 --> 00:20:43.170
At the end of the week after next, we shall be expelled from school.

00:20:44.630 --> 00:20:46.270
Wet T-shirt contest, huh?

00:20:46.510 --> 00:20:47.120
Huh?

00:20:47.940 --> 00:20:49.580
Wet T-shirt contest?

00:20:49.580 --> 00:20:52.430
You mean when girls in T-shirts get splashed with water, right?

00:20:52.430 --> 00:20:53.370
Yeah.

00:20:53.370 --> 00:20:55.530
Apparently, they do that
during seaside school.

00:20:57.230 --> 00:21:00.590
For a moment, on my
way back to the school,

00:21:00.590 --> 00:21:04.040
the image of a wet T-shirt contest flashed through my mind.

00:21:04.040 --> 00:21:06.790
I thought to myself,
"What was that?" so I turned around,

00:21:07.130 --> 00:21:08.580
and saw this van coming towards me...

00:21:09.060 --> 00:21:12.710
If it hadn't been for that,
I'd probably have been run over.

00:21:13.210 --> 00:21:14.360
What?!

00:21:14.360 --> 00:21:17.260
To think that our hearts
really did reach you...!

00:21:17.260 --> 00:21:18.710
It is a miracle!

00:21:18.710 --> 00:21:19.300
For real?

00:21:19.680 --> 00:21:20.610
That's awesome.

00:21:20.610 --> 00:21:22.260
Miracles <i>do</i> happen, huh?

00:21:22.920 --> 00:21:26.140
So you became taken with Shingo, and told him the truth?

00:21:26.940 --> 00:21:29.770
You're the captain of the guard, what were you thinking?

00:21:30.960 --> 00:21:32.650
I'm terribly sorry.

00:21:33.500 --> 00:21:34.320
Well, no matter.

00:21:34.320 --> 00:21:35.120
Huh?

00:21:35.840 --> 00:21:38.110
The DTO still ended up being successful.

00:21:38.620 --> 00:21:40.460
I shall not press you any further.

00:21:40.460 --> 00:21:41.770
No, but I—

00:21:41.770 --> 00:21:43.440
I said it is all right.

00:21:44.100 --> 00:21:44.620
Go on.

00:21:45.070 --> 00:21:45.930
Yes.

00:21:45.930 --> 00:21:47.500
You don't have to shut the door.

00:21:47.850 --> 00:21:48.820
Um...

00:21:48.820 --> 00:21:50.980
Vice President, I'm sorry.

00:21:50.980 --> 00:21:53.000
It's okay. Go.

00:21:53.430 --> 00:21:55.520
Are you sure, President?

00:21:55.520 --> 00:21:58.250
She knows about the DTO.

00:21:58.250 --> 00:22:01.260
She should probably be kept under
observation until the boys are expelled.

00:22:01.260 --> 00:22:02.560
Indeed.

00:22:02.560 --> 00:22:05.220
Leave it to you, President, to consider even that.

00:22:05.670 --> 00:22:08.090
Vice President, are you sure you don't need a hand?

00:22:08.090 --> 00:22:09.220
I'm fine.

00:22:09.220 --> 00:22:11.440
I can get out of this by myself.

00:22:11.440 --> 00:22:13.140
Hang in there, Vice President.

00:22:13.140 --> 00:22:14.900
You're almost there, Vice President.

00:22:15.980 --> 00:22:17.610
My fingertips have no strength left.

00:22:18.040 --> 00:22:18.990
I'll just have to...

00:22:25.130 --> 00:22:26.700
Miracles don't happen
by just sitting around.

00:22:27.170 --> 00:22:29.040
We have to make them happen ourselves.

00:22:29.480 --> 00:22:31.510
Just like we kept Shingo from having that accident.

00:22:32.180 --> 00:22:35.590
Truly, Shingo-dono's tale
is a miraculous one.

00:22:35.980 --> 00:22:38.550
Are we just going to give up on that wet T-shirt contest?!

00:22:39.130 --> 00:22:41.460
There's no way we can give up on it!

00:22:41.460 --> 00:22:43.170
But, what are we supposed to do?

00:22:43.170 --> 00:22:46.550
Chiyo-chan said there was a project plan for the DTO, didn't she?

00:22:46.550 --> 00:22:47.880
If we can just find that...

00:22:47.880 --> 00:22:50.730
But that's already been
disposed of, hasn't it?

00:22:51.720 --> 00:22:52.810
Yeah, well...

00:22:54.530 --> 00:22:54.980
I've...

00:22:56.980 --> 00:22:59.810
seen "DTO" someplace before...

00:24:35.390 --> 00:24:37.380
Next time on Prison School:

00:24:38.520 --> 00:24:39.830
"Full of Bodily Fluids."
